WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
The Rose of Versailles

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
The Rose of Versailles

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.900
Draw your sword.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.710
I can't forgive you no matter what!

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.670
Very well.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.620
It doesn't seem to matter what I say to you.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:28.630
Oscar...!

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.950
<i>There was a man who had sold his gun.</i>

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:09.020
<i>The man was a member of the French Guards
Company B, which Oscar commands,</i>

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.430
<i>and he had sold his gun to a pawnshop in Paris.</i>

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.570
<i>If a soldier were to sell the gun
issued to him by his country,</i>

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:20.190
<i>it would mean execution by firing squad,
regardless of his reasons.</i>

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.500
Military Police!

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.930
Is there a man named Lazare Dressel here?!

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.950
<i>The company men believed it
was their commander's doing.</i>

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:33.810
<i>That Oscar had sold him out to the authorities.</i>

