00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.140
episode

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.140
"Prelude

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.140
to the Storm"

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.590
Yield, now.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.290
You can't win with a broken sword.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:40.930
Speak for yourself.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:44.450
This is where a real man's battle begins!

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.750
<i>He's good!</i>

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.980
<i>I've never met such a formidable
swordsman before!</i>

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.050
<i>He's still confident even with a broken sword!</i>

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.300
Now's your chance, Alain!

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.270
Alain! Get her!

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.180
You idiot, Alain! That was your chance!

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:38.180
Get her! Her right arm is probably still numb!

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:40.150
Hey! What's wrong, Alain?!

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:41.340
Alain, you almost have her—!

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.300
Shut up!

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.390
Quit jabbering already!

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.390
The fight is over.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.120
And unfortunately, I lost.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.760
I hate to say this after I lost, but...

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.040
Please!

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:06.640
Have a little heart for the man who's going to be
executed by firing squad, just for selling his gun.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:07.660
To tell you the truth,

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.250
I've sold my gun, as well.
And not just once or twice!

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:15.350
I didn't sell them in a way the Military Police
would find out, like Lazare did, but still...

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.690
All these guys are in the same boat as me!

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:21.500
Sabers are a given, but some of them have
even sold off their military uniforms!

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.470
Can a noble like you understand why?!

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.730
We've all got families!

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.940
We have hungry little brothers and
sisters waiting back at home!

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.370
Some of us even save our dinner
bread and meat we get here,

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.900
and hand them to our families on visitor's days!

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.540
Do you get it?!

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.710
We put our lives on the line for this job,
but we still can't feed our families!

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:46.620
So think about that.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:50.250
You nobles like to take charge
of soldiers, so why not help one?

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.660
This is a difficult thing you're asking me.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.600
Yes, but please.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:01.470
Not only that, he's already been
arrested by the Military Police...

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:04.400
That is why I've come to ask
for your help, General Bouillé.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:10.680
Please grant him mercy as a reward for
Company B's merit, protecting Duke Ardelos.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:14.050
And as such, my subordinate's
misconduct is my responsibility!

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.350
Wait, wait...

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.190
Stop right there. You're impatient,
just like your father.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.610
Brother!

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:25.610
Diane!

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.360
Hey! Alain's sister is here!

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.320
Are you serious?!

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:38.330
Diane, your eyes are sparkling today.
What's going on?

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:43.630
Brother, I'm...

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.200
...getting married.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.590
I'm getting married!

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:49.980
I see...

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:53.180
Well, damn! When did you
find such a nice bastard?

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.040
He's tall, just like you.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.660
Aiming high, eh?

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:00.850
And... And he's very kind, as well.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.060
Thank you, Brother... for everything until now...

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:06.660
You idiot. Don't be silly.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.830
I'm going to be happy.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:10.780
Damn right, you are!

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:15.310
Hey, I'll be sure to go home on my next day off.

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:18.240
Make sure you introduce me to that
brave fellow of yours. You hear me?

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.800
Yes, definitely!

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:25.210
See you, Brother!

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:44.900
Did you see your brother?

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.110
Yes!

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.490
My brother told me this.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:58.440
He said ''Oscar'' means
''God and Sword'' in Hebrew.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:04.660
God, sword... and gorgeous blonde hair...

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:07.380
Like the Gods depicted in the frescos...

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.090
What am I saying?

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.090
I'm sorry. Please excuse me.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:16.990
Goodbye!

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:30.350
Congratulations, Alain.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.040
I hear your sister is getting married.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.920
That aside, everyone is heartbroken.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.070
She had a lot of admirers in
Company B, didn't she?

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:42.220
I feel like it's been so long since
I've heard such cheerful news.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:44.130
What's wrong?

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:46.700
You look as though your lover
was stolen away by another man.

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:48.470
You're on the mark.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.800
Honestly, I don't know what to say.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.040
Strange, isn't it?

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:55.840
I always thought of her as just a kid and
next thing I knew, she was all grown up.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.210
I see.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:01.200
So even the mightiest soldier in
Company B has a soft spot, eh?

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.480
Hey, Alain!

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:03.980
Alain!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.020
He's back! Lazare is back!

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:07.730
What?!

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:08.990
He's back!

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:10.190
He didn't get executed!

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:12.030
The Military Police acquitted him and let him go!

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:17.760
I'm back.

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:18.700
Long time no see, everyone.

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:19.930
Lazare!

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.170
What a surprise!

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:24.170
You're the first one to ever come back after
being taken away by the Military Police!

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:29.000
The interrogation was rough,
so I'm exhausted, but...

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:35.930
Lazare!

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:37.350
Squad Leader!

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:38.590
I've just returned!

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.820
I heard you were acquitted!

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:41.560
Is it true?!

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.150
It's true!

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:44.020
I'm not lying!

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:47.890
That woman commander asked General Bouillé
to use his influence over the Military Police!

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.830
What?! That woman commander did?!

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.900
You mean she wasn't the one who
sold you out to the Military Police?

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.200
I see.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.360
Go figure!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:00.200
What is it?

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:04.160
Lazare is back.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:05.370
I see.

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:06.440
Thank you.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.040
And I'm sorry.

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:09.210
It's all right.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.090
Now we can sell our guns freely.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.470
If I get caught, help me out too, all right?

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:14.470
What?!

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.430
I'm kidding.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:21.110
See you.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:28.800
André.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:29.560
Yes.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.210
You're off duty tonight, aren't you?

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:31.910
Yes.

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:33.410
Then, come with me.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:36.280
I have to go thank General Bouillé about today.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:41.040
Dress properly and represent the Company.

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:41.040
Understood!

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:46.880
Take us to Paris.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:52.590
Why are we going to Paris?

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.400
General Bouillé's manor is...

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:56.860
He's at the Opera House tonight.

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:07.390
Hey, I haven't seen André at all.
Anyone know where he is?

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:10.010
He accompanied the Commander
and went to Paris.

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:13.780
Yeah, looking like some wise guy,
riding in a gaudy noble's carriage.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:17.360
They went to Paris in a noble's carriage?

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.350
That's dangerous.

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:24.000
Paris is full of thugs, who'll attack at
the very sight of a noble these days.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:25.860
Oh, there we go.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:26.990
I'm out.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:29.030
I got beat again!

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.230
Fine, take the pot as Diane's wedding gift!

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:34.040
You idiot! We're collecting that separately!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:34.700
What?!

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:35.510
You've got to be kidding me!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.600
Come on, don't be stingy!

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:55.520
See that?

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:56.820
It's a noble's carriage.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.190
They're nobles!

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:07.220
Drag them out!

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:09.490
Grab him!

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:11.060
Wait!

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.730
André isn't a noble!

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.390
André!!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.800
Oscar!!

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:28.940
Burn it!

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:38.320
<i>André isn't a noble!</i>

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.460
<i>Don't harm that man!</i>

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:43.340
Opera House

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:49.330
General Bouillé.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:53.400
A report has just come in that a riot has
broken out in the Saint-Antoine district.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:58.260
To avoid any danger, perhaps it's best for you
\hto cut your visit short and return to Versailles.

00:13:58.260 --> 00:13:59.450
I'll take your suggestion, then.

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:03.580
Colonel, you brought a platoon with you, correct?

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:04.280
Yes!

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.250
Then, guarding me won't be necessary.

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:07.990
I want you to go quell the riot.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.240
Understood!

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.330
You, explain the situation in more detail.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:18.530
Yes! Armed with clubs, approximately 200
residents of the Saint-Antoine district,

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:20.430
have attacked a noble's carriage.

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:23.420
According to the report, the crest on the
carriage was a blue lion holding a sword.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.270
What?!

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:25.700
A blue lion holding a sword?!

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:27.470
Yes, Colonel Fersen!

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:28.840
<i>It's the Jarjayes family crest!</i>

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:29.870
<i>Could it be...?!</i>

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:30.670
<i>Oscar!</i>

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:35.110
Army Cavalry Division, 105th Platoon!

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:37.010
Advance to Saint-Antoine district!

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:43.530
He's trying escape!

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:47.530
Don't let him get away!

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.260
Beat him to death!

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:56.070
Come back here!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.090
Back off, you scoundrels!

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:03.370
Damn!

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:04.170
It's the military!

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:10.680
Oscar!

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:17.590
Oscar!

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:18.730
Pull yourself together! Oscar!

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:21.440
Fersen...

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:24.020
Thank goodness... you're all right.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:29.000
André!

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.130
Where's André?!

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:32.050
André!

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.020
Wait, Oscar!

00:15:32.020 --> 00:15:33.070
If you go, they'll attack you again!

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:34.810
Let me go! André is...!

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:36.370
My André is in danger!

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:37.540
What?!

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.330
My... André?!

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:42.540
All right.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:45.680
You stay here.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:47.520
Your... Your André...

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:48.800
I swear I'll save him!

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.050
My... André...

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:01.630
André!

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:03.230
André!!

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:08.670
Hang him!

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:10.200
Hang the noble!

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:23.120
Rioters, clear your ears and listen closely!

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.290
My name is Hans Axel von Fersen!

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:27.290
Hans Axel von Fersen?

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:28.660
Fersen...?

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:30.760
Oh, he's Antoinette's lover!

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:32.030
That's right!

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:33.680
He's that womanizer, Fersen!

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.220
Everyone, hang him! Hang him first!

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:42.800
Don't let him escape!

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:05.760
My Lady, I've brought you some hot chocolate.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.130
Thank you.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:10.470
What a harrowing thing you went through.

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:15.760
I'm too afraid to go shopping
by myself in Paris these days.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.710
How are André's injuries?

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:20.510
He has 36 bruises all over his body!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:23.510
But he's saying he's going to do his
best to return to the barracks in 3 days.

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:24.850
I see.

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.950
I'm glad his injuries weren't severe
as I had thought. I'm really glad...

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:31.410
It's really been awhile since
you had some time off, hasn't it?

00:17:32.390 --> 00:17:33.460
It really has.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.780
What injury should I get for my next day off?

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:38.130
Wha—?! My Lady, you already
have 12 bruises yourself!

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:39.360
It isn't funny!

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:40.490
Excuse me!

00:17:41.130 --> 00:17:42.930
Nanna, your hot chocolate is delicious.

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:44.090
It's very delicious...

00:17:48.740 --> 00:17:50.510
<i>Let me go! André is...!</i>

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:51.940
<i>My André is in danger!</i>

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:54.610
<i>My André is in danger!</i>

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:06.140
We just received word that Count Fersen returned
safely to the army barracks last night.

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:07.690
I see.

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:09.960
How about some hot chocolate?

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:11.290
No, I'm all right.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:26.300
<i>Back then, I definitely would have
gone to save Fersen from the mob.</i>

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.430
Don't you think it's odd though?

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.590
Maybe something happened?

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:45.970
Alain is...?

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:51.950
Yes, he took some time off for his sister's
wedding a week ago, but hasn't returned.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.900
He's never taken a leave without
prior consent, so...

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.910
It's really odd.

00:18:57.910 --> 00:18:59.380
He hasn't even come to get his pay.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:01.480
He has a sick mother, doesn't he?

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:04.020
He said her medicine costs a lot.

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:05.540
I wonder what happened?

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:08.250
Oscar.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.000
Could I get permission to go out?

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:13.190
I want to deliver Alain his pay.

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:14.620
Wait, André.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:17.210
I'll go with you.

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:28.230
26 Belleville Street.
It should be around here.

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.190
Hey, you two, are you going to Alain's apartment?

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:37.650
Yes, we are.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:41.610
Then, tell Alain to do something
about this stench for me.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:42.820
Stench?

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:44.160
Yeah.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.660
He probably bought a bunch of cheap meat.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:51.290
If he's going to let it rot, he could have shared
it with his neighbors! So inconsiderate!

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:55.260
Now that she mentioned it,
something does smell odd.

00:19:58.680 --> 00:19:59.700
Alain!

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:01.010
It's André!

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:02.310
I've brought your pay!

00:20:02.310 --> 00:20:03.600
Alain, I'm coming in.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:14.310
Are you Alain's mother?

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:15.940
Yes...

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:18.400
Alain... Where is Alain?

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:22.230
He's by Diane's side...
Been there this whole time...

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:25.530
Alain loved his sister dearly...

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:39.370
Diane was betrayed by her love...

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:43.380
The man was a poor noble.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.880
The day before their wedding,

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:51.490
he suddenly received a proposal
from a rich man's daughter,

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:53.560
and he left my daughter for her...

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:59.150
My daughter loved him, believed in
him and devoted her all to him...

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:05.030
He deserted my daughter, as through he
were throwing away some leftover coffee...

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:13.110
Poor thing, it must have been so
painful when she hung herself...

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.950
Sorry, but I won't be going back
to the French Guards for a while.

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:23.950
Her gentle smile and cheerful voice
are gone from this world...

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:28.330
Until... Until I'm able to come to
terms with that, I won't leave...

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:30.470
I won't leave her side...!

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:42.450
The Estates-General!

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:43.310
The Estates-General!

00:21:43.310 --> 00:21:45.680
Convene the Estates-General!

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:47.510
The Estates-General!

00:21:47.510 --> 00:21:51.000
Send our representatives to the general assembly!

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:55.150
<i>"Convene the Estates-General"...</i>

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:56.420
<i>The Estates-General...</i>

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:58.750
<i>The Third Estate, the commoner's class,</i>

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:01.360
<i>consisted of everyone except
the nobles and the clergy.</i>

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:04.730
<i>Their protest was a movement to send their
representatives to the general assembly.</i>

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:11.500
<i>The death of Alain's sister, Diane and the
changing of the times hardly seemed related.</i>

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:15.310
<i>Yet, a sense of foreboding crossed Oscar's mind.</i>

00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:22.510
<i>"Those who are beautiful, loved dearly, and should
be alive, can one day be suddenly lost forever."</i>

00:22:22.510 --> 00:22:28.150
<i>"Perhaps the new era would also be a tragic one,"
she thought to herself.</i>

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:33.290
To be continued

